  "description": "• Formation of a new structural opening at outrigger level to accommodate French-style doors, improving\nconnectivity between internal accommodation and the rear garden.\n• Conversion of the loft to create additional habitable accommodation, including the construction of one\nmodest rear dormer and one small side dormer, both designed to remain subordinate to the principal roof form.\n• Replacement of existing single-glazed sash windows with high-quality, double-glazed sash windows\nmatching the original profiles and detailing.\n•Removal of an existing side entrance door and introduction of a new side window within the side passage to\nimprove functionality and internal light.\n•The existing rear window located at the outrigger will be increased in width to improve proportion, visual\nbalance and internal daylight provision.\n•Installation of two conservation-style rooflights (Velux type) to the roof slope. These will be flush-fitting\nconservation units set within the roof plane to minimise visual impact and preserve the character of the property\nwithin the conservation area.\n•Removal of the redundant chimney stack located at the rear outrigger roof. The alteration is limited to the rear\nelevation and will not be visible from the public realm, resulting in no harm to the character or appearance of the\nbuilding.\n• Installation of a new modest pedestrian gate and widened vehicular access gate to the front boundary.",
